{"text": "Timeline of First Security Corporation major bank merger partners\nSelections only, not a complete list\n\n1928\ne First Security Corporation, the first multistate bank holding company, was created with\n17 banks and one building and loan company, which included First National Bank of\nOgden and Ogden Savings Bank\n1929\ne Merged with National Copper Bank of Salt Lake City to beomce First National Bank of\nSalt Lake City\n1932\ne Acquires Deseret National Bank\n1933\ne Anderson Brothers Bank and First Security Bank of Jerome become First Security Bank\nof Idaho\n1948\ne First Security Trust Company in Salt Lake City, the result of merger between Bankers\nTrust Company and Central Trust Company in 1931, was acquired by First Security\nCorporation\n1964\ne First Security Bank of Twin Falls was acquired by First Security Bank of Idaho, NA\n1977\ne First Security Bank of Utah, NA acquired First Security Bank of Bountiful, NA\n1980-81\ne First Security Bank of Utah, NA acquired First Security Bank of Logan, First Security\nBank of Murray, First Security Bank of Richfield, First Security Bank of Orem\n1990\ne Acquired Deseret Bancorporation (UT)\n1993\ne Acquired First Bankshares, Inc., Deseret Southwest Community Bancorp, First National\nFinancial Corporation, Continental Bancorporation\ne First Security Bank of Rock Springs renamed First Security Bank of Wyoming, NA\n1996\ne First Security Bank of Utah changes name to First Security Bank, NA\ne First Security Bank, NA acquires First Security Bank of Idaho, NA\n1997\n\nFirst Security Bank, NA acquires First Security Bank of Wyoming, NA\n\nAcquired American Bancorp of Nevada\nFirst Security/Page 1 of 2",
